From: Johann Hartmann <johann@mayflower.de>
Subject: [PATCH] media: uvcvideo: keep noncoherent URBs within DMA segment limit

usb_alloc_noncoherent() allocates a DMA-mapped buffer for each UVC URB. The
size is page rounded by dma_alloc_noncontiguous(), which can exceed the host
controller's advertised maximum DMA segment size even when the requested
payload is slightly smaller.

On the N1X P16, an attached Logitech StreamCam MJPEG stream on XHCI
NVDA8000:00 requests 32 packets of 3072 bytes (98304 bytes). That DMA
mapping exceeds the host's 65536-byte maximum and triggers DMA-debug. Limit
packets per URB using the USB host DMA device's segment limit, rounded down
to complete pages. Keep the existing retry-on-allocation-failure path and
fail cleanly if even one packet cannot fit.

Signed-off-by: Johann Hartmann <johann@mayflower.de>
---
 drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
@@ -1840,6 +1840,9 @@
 	unsigned int size, unsigned int psize, gfp_t gfp_flags)
 {
 	unsigned int npackets;
+	unsigned int max_packets;
+	unsigned int max_seg_size;
+	struct device *dma_dev;
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	/* Buffers are already allocated, bail out. */
@@ -1853,6 +1856,19 @@
 	npackets = DIV_ROUND_UP(size, psize);
 	if (npackets > UVC_MAX_PACKETS)
 		npackets = UVC_MAX_PACKETS;
+
+	/* The noncoherent DMA allocation is page rounded and one DMA segment. */
+	dma_dev = bus_to_hcd(stream->dev->udev->bus)->self.sysdev;
+	max_seg_size = dma_get_max_seg_size(dma_dev);
+	max_packets = round_down(max_seg_size, PAGE_SIZE) / psize;
+	if (!max_packets)
+		return 0;
+	if (npackets > max_packets) {
+		uvc_dbg(stream->dev, VIDEO,
+			 "Limiting URB to %u packets (DMA max %u bytes)\n",
+			 max_packets, max_seg_size);
+		npackets = max_packets;
+	}
 
 	/* Retry allocations until one succeed. */
 	for (; npackets > 0; npackets /= 2) {
